%% SMART-HORIZON — Technical Architecture (full pipeline)
%% Paste into https://mermaid.live or import into Excalidraw (Mermaid-to-Excalidraw).
flowchart TB

    N1["<b>INPUT DATA</b>
    6 delivered CSVs — GEO + MEO, train + test
    utc_time, x/y/z error (m), clock error (m)
    orbit label only — no satellite ID"]

    N2["<b>INGESTION &amp; CLEANING</b>  ·  sih.py
    lossless de-duplication (verified one backward step)
    parse, sort, drop mis-dated rows
    gap-aware, native irregular sampling (no interpolation)"]

    N3["<b>DATA DIAGNOSIS</b>  ·  experiments.py
    ~50% duplicate rows, coverage 13–32%, min test = 6 pts
    day-8 distribution shift (2.5–17× variance), volatility ramp
    GEO sign-flip artefact flagged"]

    N4["<b>ML BASELINE TEST</b>  ·  experiments.py
    6 standard models (Ridge, KNN, RF, GBM, SVR, MLP)
    27k rows, 19 engineered features → all plateau at baseline
    ⇒ inputs don't determine output → need external info"]

    N5["<b>PHYSICS DERIVATION</b>  ·  PHYSICS.md
    orbit class → period (GEO sidereal, MEO per-constellation)
    ECEF ⊗ Earth rotation → beat frequencies
    x,y split into two beats; z keeps orbital period
    clock = random walk + resets → no harmonics on clock
    periods verified on periodogram before fitting"]

    N6["<b>SYNTHETIC GENERATOR</b>  ·  synth.py
    physics → data engine: beats + drift + noise + clock RW
    sampled at real irregular timestamps
    120 windows with known day-8
    purpose: validation, not training"]

    N7["<b>SMART-HORIZON MODEL</b>  ·  model.py
    hypothesis space fixed by physics (admissible periods)
    per-window period: gap-tolerant Lomb-Scargle, corridor-bounded
    beat periods derived by formula, not searched
    candidates: level estimators + harmonic orders
    basis chosen by held-out day-7 self-validation
    ridge regression on all 7 days, runaway clamp
    outputs mean + 1σ, no stored weights (fits per window)"]

    N8["<b>SCORING</b>  ·  sw_score.py
    reverse-engineered Shapiro-Francia (kurtosis-switching)
    validated vs organiser benchmark (W 0.981, p 0.584)
    reports W, p, H (Priority 1) + mean/std (Priority 2)"]

    N9["<b>VALIDATION RESULTS</b>
    synthetic: beats do-nothing 78% GEO / 51% MEO (120 windows)
    real MEO: 57% &amp; 19% better, beats answer-key oracle
    real GEO: 0.3% oracle → file corrupt, reproduced by injection"]

    N10["<b>OUTPUT</b>  ·  predict.py
    7 days in → day-8 on 15-min grid
    prediction + 1σ per channel at arbitrary timestamps"]

    N1 --> N2 --> N3 --> N4 --> N5
    N5 --> N6
    N5 --> N7
    N6 -. validates .-> N7
    N7 --> N8 --> N9 --> N10

